# Architecture

```text
                    ┌──────────────────────┐
                    │ FastAPI / MCP Client │
                    └──────────┬───────────┘
                               │
                    ┌──────────▼───────────┐
                    │ Stateless Orchestrator│
                    └──────────┬───────────┘
                               │ asyncio.gather
             ┌─────────────────┼──────────────────┐
             ▼                 ▼                  ▼
      Academic Agent     Semantic RAG Agent   Graph Agent
          arXiv             ChromaDB            Neo4j
             └─────────────────┼──────────────────┘
                               ▼
                     Evidence Ranker/Verifier
                               ▼
                       Gemini Synthesis
                               ▼
                    Cited Research Report
```

## Scalability

Workers contain no user/session state. Persistent state is externalized to ChromaDB and Neo4j. The AWS ECS task definition uses multiple Fargate replicas (`desired_count`) so identical workers can be scaled horizontally.

## Retrieval

ChromaDB is configured with cosine distance and HNSW indexing. Retrieval scores are normalized from Chroma distance to a cosine-similarity-style relevance score. The evaluation harness reports Precision@K, Recall@K, and MRR.

## Graph reasoning

Neo4j stores entities and relationships. `bfs_entity_neighborhood` expands the relationship frontier by shortest traversal depth, making the BFS behavior explicit and testable.

## MCP

`app/mcp/server.py` exposes research, semantic retrieval, entity lookup, and graph-BFS tools through the Model Context Protocol.
